Z||000037||thomas_l||04-06-2001||09:28 AM||||My angry 87 GT autocross project just got dropped by the tow truck yesterday. It's a buy here-pay here repo with the air transmission (i.e. none) and optional mildew upholstery. Parts are coming - this weekend I am attacking the stinky interior and next weekend its transmission time!<P>I bought the Fiero so I won't break my daily driver '00 Lincoln LS at the track. Something tells me the Fiero will be less expensive to fix.<P>And last but not least, my wife has a '01 C240 which is mildly sporty but definitely not a racer.||||reg||1
Z||000038||WKDFIRO||04-06-2001||07:09 PM||||I drive a white 87 coupe automatic, sometimes. Its stock but after 276,000 miles its in need of some cleaning up...<P>My baby is the 85 GT (I guess that would make ME anthony_85gt!) its been my work in progress...<P>Engine:<BR>-Block/heads painted red<BR>-Match ported (Intake/exhaust)<BR>-Roller tip rockers<BR>-3 angle valve job<BR>-Babe Erson Cam<BR>-RAM AIR intake (utilizing Holley style  scoop and a straight pipe going to the air filter canister...haven't decided how Im going to replace the canister)<BR>-2.5 inch mandrel bent exhaust from the cat back going to Megs 4.5 inch round roll tipped exhaust.<BR>-Powder coated:<BR>  Intake plenum (after the casting flash was taken off.<BR>  Valve covers (they needed to be redone)<BR>-Polished/chromed:<BR>  Intake plenum/valve covers<BR>  Throttle body (hard to keep polished too!)<BR>  Torque sturt/brackets (they really look nice when its done.)<BR>(Special thanks to Keith "Fiero Doc" Huff, John Parenti and Bob York for help with the engine and polishing/chroming and powder coating!)<P>Suspension:<P>-Urethane:<BR>   Control arms<BR>   Sway bar (front, haven't saved up for the back.)<BR>   Cradle mounts<P>-Lowered 2 inches in front 1 1/2 inches in back. (real subtle slant)<P>-Image 16x7 wheels originally with 225/50 BF Goodrich Comp TA VR4 (love them but saving up for new ones. Have some no names on now.)<P>-Rear cross drilled rotors (saving up for the fronts...but now thinking upgrade...)<P>Interior:<P>-Custom Shortend shifter (Thanks Chris Sideris!) with leather knob from Camaro (only for show)<BR>-Technics AM/FM/CD/Tape player (I love having the choice!<BR>-120 mph speedo<BR>-manual fan switch<BR>-Custom TTH (Torn To Hell)High Performance Driver's seat. <P><BR>Exterior:<BR>-Hi Performance PPG (Paint Peeling Godawful!)Black (Though peeling to red alarmingly fast...big thanks to the former owner!)<BR>-Formula nose and tail<BR>-Love my sunroof! (That was stock)<BR>-87-88 Headlights (The quiet, easy to rebuild ones  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">...)<P>Wow, thats all Ive done in the past 5 years Ive had it...<P>And my "Grownup" car is a 99 Grand Prix GT.||||reg||1
